# F-228 fix: the Vercel CLI does NOT read .gitignore — it only reads this
# file (and .nowignore), and its own built-in default list only excludes
# .env.local / .env.*.local. Without this file, `vercel --prod` (run from
# scripts/go-live.mjs) uploaded the developer's real `.env` — production DB
# URL, Supabase secret key, Cloudflare/R2 keys, OpenAI key, admin seed
# password, all of it — into the deployment's source, every time.
#
# scripts/go-live.mjs refuses to deploy if this file goes missing or stops
# covering the .env family (see scripts/lib/deploy-checks.mjs's
# vercelIgnoreCoversEnvSecrets, unit-tested in deploy-checks.test.ts).
.env
.env.*
!.env*.example

# Dev-only artifacts that were also found inside the current production
# deployment's source (see F-228's evidence) — none of them are needed to
# build or run the app.
.claude/
bin/cloudflared.exe
dogfood-output/
.lighthouseci/
*.tsbuildinfo
